<sn><md>### Example Operations {.text-center}

##### Copy Files

```bash
rclone copy mega:Documents gdrive:Documents
```

Copies files from MEGA to Google Drive without deleting the originals.

```text
MEGA:Documents  ──────────→  Google Drive:Documents
     Source                    Destination
```

---

##### Move Files

```bash
rclone move mega:Documents gdrive:Documents
```

Transfers files to Google Drive and removes the originals from MEGA after a successful transfer.

---

##### Sync Files

```bash
rclone sync mega:Documents gdrive:Documents
```

Makes the Google Drive destination match the MEGA source.

⚠️ Files in the destination that don't exist in the source may be deleted.

---

##### Check Files

```bash
rclone check mega:Documents gdrive:Documents
```

Compares files between the two cloud locations.

---

##### Preview Before Running

Use `--dry-run`:

```bash
rclone sync mega:Documents gdrive:Documents --dry-run
```

This lets you preview the operation without making any actual changes.
